  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Mormon",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 3,
    "summary": "Mormon cries repentance unto the Nephites—They gain a great victory and glory in their own strength—Mormon refuses to lead them, and his prayers for them are without faith—The Book of Mormon invites the twelve tribes of Israel to believe the gospel. About A.D. 360–62.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that the Lamanites did not come to battle again until ten years more had passed away. And behold, I had employed my people, the Nephites, in preparing their lands and their arms against the time of battle.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mormon 3:1",
        "book": "Mormon",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that the Lord did say unto me: Cry unto this people—Repent ye, and come unto me, and be ye baptized, and build up again my church, and ye shall be spared.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 167,
            "end": 173,
            "text": "Hel. 15:17 (16–17); Morm. 6:11 (11–15)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mormon 3:2",
        "book": "Mormon",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And I did cry unto this people, but it was in vain; and they did not realize that it was the Lord that had spared them, and granted unto them a chance for repentance. And behold they did harden their hearts against the Lord their God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "Morm. 4:18."
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 76,
            "text": "TG Hardheartedness; Ingratitude."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
